    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "2590a1f88ab5a5176e92b15845ac38a810b6dfec",
      "subject": "Add a shared optimizer-intelligence layer as the single interpretation path for compatible execution-shape evidence. Regression dispatch and in-job shape resolution now use the same measured-first, predicted-second policy: compatible measured evidence on the requested runner wins, otherwise cross-vCPU prediction scales pipelines linearly as `pl_current / vcpu_current * vcpu_new`, bounded by `max pipelines = vCPU` and `max threads = vCPU * 2`. This makes ARE's persisted 22p/2t shape on 32 vCPU resolve to a predicted 132p/2t on a 192-vCPU runner instead of falling back to 1p/384t. Predicted dispatch keeps the requested runner pool and is re-resolved on the concrete runner so prediction provenance is recorded normally rather than being mistaken for measured evidence. Shape prediction now imports the canonical preference selector directly from the execution-shape domain, and new contract tests cover linear scaling, measured-over-predicted precedence, pre-dispatch prediction, and concrete-runner re-resolution. All 662 tests pass."
    }
  ],
